// The connector contract (oryxa-platform#8, #9 §3). A connector is a process the connector host
// calls over gRPC, written in any language. It never holds a provider credential: every call
// carries an Egress, and the connector sends provider requests through the broker egress proxy
// (connectors/broker-proxy.json). It never publishes events or writes storage either: it emits
// changes on the Sync stream and the host validates, stores and announces them.
//
